    "violates": "output_kind stream cannot declare pagination",
    "detect": "schema",
    "at": "/commands/0/pagination",
    "why": "Pages are how a consumer walks a result that already exists. A stream is bounded from the other end: the consumer reads until it has enough and closes the pipe, and asks for less with `--since` or `--tail`. A cursor into a sequence that has no end describes a loop that never terminates."
  },
